# Definition of done

Do not report a single vague “DONE”. Use:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **IMPLEMENTED** | Code landed in repo |
| **TESTED** | Targeted + required regression passed |
| **DEPLOYED** | TEST production is serving the commit |
| **LIVE VERIFIED** | User-facing flow seen in deployed TEST UI |
| **PRODUCTION READY TEST** | All of the above for TEST; Live still off |

User-facing payment functionality **cannot** be Production Ready TEST from unit tests, code inspection, DB rows, build, or deploy SHA alone.

If Cursor cannot authenticate to the required account: **IMPLEMENTED — LIVE QA REQUIRED**, Production Ready TEST = **NO**.

Example:

- Implementation: PASS
- Unit tests: PASS
- Regression: PASS
- Deployment: PASS
- Live browser QA: NOT AVAILABLE
- Production Ready TEST: NO
